# Game-feel rules

- Every player action gets **instant local feedback** (scale punch, stamp, burst, sound)
  — never wait for the server round-trip to acknowledge a tap.
- Every score change reaches the screen only through the reveal system: `RevealEvent`s
  played sequentially, AnimatedNumber rollups, and HUD floating deltas. No silent jumps.
- Reveal events carry `animation` and `intensity` hints (shared types). Server-side code
  gets sensible defaults from `inferAnimation()` in `shared/src/game/reveal.ts`; override
  at the call site when the moment deserves more/less drama.
- Player state is broadcast through `PirateAvatar` moods (answered, nervous, attacked,
  protected, cursed, accused, winner) — extend the mood table rather than inventing
  one-off status indicators.
- Rarity presentation comes exclusively from `client/src/lib/rarityStyles.ts`. All items
  must feel distinct; legendary must feel outrageous.
- The chest ceremony (slam → chains → shake → slot spin → burst → card) is a core product
  moment. Do not shorten it below ~4s or remove stages without explicit instruction.
- Fun copy is part of game feel: "Set Sail", "Fire!", "MUTINY!", "You have been
  absolutely robbed." Keep it cheeky and 9+ friendly.
- Multiplayer stays authoritative: clients animate received state/events and never
  simulate outcomes locally before the server confirms them.
